 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? A sketch is just quick drawing, usually done quickly, a study is more detailed and takes more time, often done from life. Sort of. It' practice drawing from a real object, often at the same size as the final piece. Lovely. For that, I'd start with a quick rough drawing. The big shapes, the sky, the mountains, the horizon. Get those right before worrying about trees. Clouds are easy. A few simple lines and shades can make them look full and lazy.",
